    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191771": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Lecturer Rice University: Wiess School of Natural Sciences: Chemistry Location Houston, Texas Open Date Aug 18, 2026 Deadline Oct 01, 2026 at 11:59 PM Eastern Time Description The Department of Chemistry at Rice University in Houston, Texas, invites applications for a full-time (9-month) non-tenure track Lecturer position. The start date is July 1, 2027. This position has an initial commitment of one academic year, with renewal pending adequate performance in the first year. Depending on the candidate's qualifications, there is an opportunity for appointment to Rice’s Teaching Professor track. Teaching responsibilities will focus primarily on General Chemistry and may include lectures, laboratory courses (day and evening), and discussion sections. Additional teaching assignments may be made based on departmental needs and the candidate’s expertise. This position will work collaboratively with other faculty members to develop and teach course content and materials. Participation in departmental service and committees is possible and encouraged. Optional summer school teaching for extra compensation may be available. This position requires a doctoral degree in chemistry or a closely related field by July 1, 2027, and previous teaching experience. Preference will be given to candidates with a track record of teaching excellence (i.e., prior teaching experience and use of evidence-based practices) and experience in mentoring teaching assistants at the college/university level. Candidates must complete applications through Interfolio, the hiring system for Rice University, at the following link: https://apply.interfolio.com/191771 . In addition to the application, the following documents are required: 1) Cover Letter 2) Curriculum Vitae (CV) 3) Teaching Statement (up to 3 pages) 4) Two Letters of Recommendation (applicants must initiate requests for recommendation letters through Interfolio during the application process) Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026, and will continue until the position has been filled. Candidates are encouraged to apply before this date. Rice University, located in Houston, Texas, the 4 th largest and most diverse city in the United States, combines the research excellence of an R1 institution with the small, collaborative feel of a top liberal arts college. The Chemistry Department strives to maintain an equitable and inclusive academic environment for all of our members. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Rice University is an Equal Opportunity Employer with commitment to diversity at all levels, and considers for employment qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, genetic information, disability or protected veteran status. Rice Mission and Values : Mission and Values | Rice University © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also us